; XSparkScalp (TrendScalp) - XAUUSD M1 "$100 account" profile
; STATUS: UNTESTED AS A PROFILE. The numbers below are derived from a 19-day
; Strategy Tester log (2026.09.01-19, XAUUSDm M1, Exness-MT5Trial17, real
; ticks), but no tester run has been performed with THIS preset loaded.
;
; READ THIS FIRST: $100 IS BELOW THE SHIPPED CEILING'S VIABLE MINIMUM ON GOLD.
; This preset requires a build where XSPARK_TRENDSCALP_MAX_MIN_LOT_RISK_PCT is
; 5.0. On a build still shipping the 3.0 ceiling, InpScalpMinLotRiskCapPct
; below is clamped back to 3.0 and the EA takes ZERO trades.
;
; WHY $100 IS THE PROBLEM. On XAUUSD one lot is 100 oz, so the 0.01 broker
; minimum is 1 oz and a $1 price move is $1. Risk in dollars for the smallest
; trade therefore EQUALS the stop distance in dollars. Measured over the 602
; signals the tester refused:
;
;   XAUUSDm M1 minimum-lot risk:  min $4.00   median $4.33   max $14.89
;
;   balance    median risk    shipped 3.0 cap    signals that size
;   $100          4.33%         $3.00                 0 / 602   (0%)
;   $125          3.46%         $3.75                 0 / 602   (0%)
;   $150          2.89%         $4.50               540 / 602  (90%)
;   $200          2.17%         $6.00               581 / 602  (97%)
;   $500          0.87%        $15.00               602 / 602 (100%)
;
; At $100 the SMALLEST stop in nineteen days was already 33% over the 3.0 cap's
; budget. That is arithmetic, not tuning. The log it came from: 867 signals,
; 0 entries, final balance unchanged at 100.00.
;
; WHAT THIS PRESET ACCEPTS. A 5.0 cap admits 94% of those signals and refuses
; the widest-ATR 6%, so it doubles as a volatility filter. The price is that
; every trade risks about 4.3% of the account. Five stops in a row is -20%.
; The exit geometry is 1:1, whose no-edge win rate is 47%, and the entry's edge
; is UNMEASURED. Nothing here is a profitability claim.
;
; THE ONE RESULT WORTH KNOWING BEFORE YOU FUND THIS. In the same log, the same
; EA on the same symbol and period with a balance large enough to trade freely
; ($10,000, 118 trades, InpScalpExitStyle=0) finished at $8,831.85 - DOWN 11.7%
; in 19 days. M1 gold was net-negative in the only sample available. A $100
; account runs the same strategy at 5x the per-trade risk.
;
; BETTER OPTIONS THAN THIS PRESET, if either is open to you:
;   - A cent account. 1 lot = 1,000 units instead of 100,000, so minimum-lot
;     risk falls ~100x and the shipped 3.0 cap sizes normally at 1-2% risk.
;   - A gold symbol with a 0.001 minimum. Risk becomes ~$0.43 = 0.43% of $100
;     and the shipped default works untouched. Read SYMBOL_VOLUME_MIN for the
;     exact symbol on your account rather than assuming 0.01.
;
; CHART: attach to XAUUSD M1. Not M5/M10 - a longer period widens the stop and
; makes this WORSE, not better. The same log measured M10 minimum-lot risk at a
; median of $8.17 (8.17% of $100) against $4.33 on M1.

InpScalpEnableTrading=true

; --- inert at this balance, and left at the shipped value deliberately. A $1
;     budget cannot buy the 0.01 minimum, so the small-account cap below is
;     what actually sizes every trade. Raising this changes nothing at $100. ---
InpScalpRiskPct=1.0

; --- all sessions: at 1 open trade and ~34 signals a day, narrowing the window
;     removes trades without reducing per-trade risk ---
InpScalpSessions=0
InpScalpBrokerUtcOffset=0

; --- SET THIS TO WHAT YOUR BROKER ACTUALLY CHARGES. 0.0 is correct only on a
;     spread-only gold account. An understated figure under-counts round-trip
;     cost and admits trades the cost floor should refuse, until the live
;     verification catches the first closure. ---
InpScalpCommissionPerLot=0.0

; --- 1:1 target. The log does not separate exit styles cleanly enough on M1 to
;     recommend 1 over 0: the M5/M10 runs that used style 1 finished positive,
;     but on different timeframes, so that is confounded, not evidence. ---
InpScalpExitStyle=0

; --- THE SETTING THIS PRESET EXISTS FOR. 5.0 admits 94% of the signals the
;     3.0 default refused. Requires the raised ceiling; on an older build this
;     silently becomes 3.0 and nothing trades. Check the journal's minimum-lot
;     line on the first bar - it now warns when this cap is too low. ---
InpScalpMinLotRiskCapPct=5.0

; --- widened because per-trade risk is forced up to ~4.3%. At the shipped 6.0
;     a single stop very nearly exhausts the day and there is no second trade,
;     which defeats the point of a scalper. 15.0 tolerates 3 stops from the
;     day's peak equity; the drawdown is measured from that peak, not from the
;     day's opening balance, so a winning run raises the bar rather than
;     banking extra loss budget. ---
InpScalpMaxDailyDDPct=15.0

; --- emergency stop ON, and it must stay above the daily limit or it fires
;     first and the daily limit never acts. 30.0 latches after ~6 consecutive
;     stops. It closes everything and refuses to reopen until you clear it
;     deliberately with InpScalpClearKillswitchLatch. ---
InpScalpUseTotalDDKillSwitch=true
InpScalpMaxTotalDDPct=30.0

InpScalpMagicNumber=770333

; --- leave ON for the first weeks at this balance. Every sizing refusal is
;     logged at DEBUG; with this off, a blocked run looks identical to a quiet
;     one. This is exactly how the 867-signal/0-trade run went unnoticed. ---
InpScalpVerboseLog=true

InpScalpClearKillswitchLatch=false
